{"id":"mahabharata-4-061","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · The Kauravas stupefied","summary":{"en":"Stung by the taunt, Duryodhana turns back, and all the Kaurava warriors surround Arjuna again. Arjuna looses the stupefying weapon, and they all fall senseless; remembering the princess's request, he sends Uttara to take the fine upper garments of Drona, Kripa, Karna, Ashvatthaman and Duryodhana, leaving Bhishma, who knows the counter-weapon, untouched, and then turns for home.","kn":"ಹಂಗಿನಿಂದ ನೊಂದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಹಿಂದಿರುಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಎಲ್ಲ ಕೌರವವೀರರೂ ಮತ್ತೆ ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ಸುತ್ತುವರಿಯುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಸಮ್ಮೋಹನಾಸ್ತ್ರ ಪ್ರಯೋಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ಪ್ರಜ್ಞೆತಪ್ಪಿ ಬೀಳುತ್ತಾರೆ; ರಾಜಕುಮಾರಿಯ ಕೋರಿಕೆ ನೆನೆದು ದ್ರೋಣ, ಕೃಪ, ಕರ್ಣ, ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನರ ಉತ್ತರೀಯಗಳನ್ನು ತರಲು ಉತ್ತರನನ್ನು ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಪ್ರತ್ಯಸ್ತ್ರ ಬಲ್ಲ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಮುಟ್ಟದೆ ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಮನೆಗೆ ತಿರುಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"ताने से आहत दुर्योधन लौट आता है, और सब कौरव योद्धा फिर अर्जुन को घेर लेते हैं। अर्जुन सम्मोहन अस्त्र छोड़ते हैं, और सब मूर्च्छित होकर गिर पड़ते हैं; राजकुमारी की माँग याद कर वे उत्तर को द्रोण, कृप, कर्ण, अश्वत्थामा और दुर्योधन के सुन्दर उत्तरीय लाने भेजते हैं, प्रति-अस्त्र जानने वाले भीष्म को छोड़ देते हैं, और फिर घर की ओर मुड़ते हैं।","te":"ఎత్తిపొడుపుకు నొచ్చుకున్న దుర్యోధనుడు వెనుదిరుగుతాడు, కౌరవవీరులందరూ మళ్లీ అర్జునుని చుట్టుముడతారు. అర్జునుడు సమ్మోహనాస్త్రం ప్రయోగిస్తాడు, అందరూ స్పృహ తప్పి పడిపోతారు; రాజకుమారి కోరిక గుర్తుచేసుకొని ద్రోణుడు, కృపుడు, కర్ణుడు, అశ్వత్థామ, దుర్యోధనుల ఉత్తరీయాలను తేవడానికి ఉత్తరుని పంపుతాడు, ప్రతిఅస్త్రం తెలిసిన భీష్ముని తాకకుండా వదిలి ఇంటికి తిరుగుతాడు.","ta":"ஏளனத்தால் புண்பட்ட துரியோதனன் திரும்ப, கௌரவ வீரர்கள் அனைவரும் மீண்டும் அர்ஜுனனைச் சூழ்கிறார்கள். அர்ஜுனன் மயக்க அஸ்திரத்தை ஏவ, அனைவரும் மயங்கி விழுகிறார்கள்; இளவரசியின் வேண்டுகோளை நினைத்து த்ரோணர், க்ருபர், கர்ணன், அஶ்வத்தாமா, துரியோதனனின் அழகிய மேலாடைகளை எடுத்து வர உத்தரனை அனுப்பி, எதிர் அஸ்திரம் அறிந்த பீஷ்மரைத் தொடாமல் விட்டு, வீடு நோக்கித் திரும்புகிறான்.","ml":"പരിഹാസം കൊണ്ട് വാശി കയറിയ ദുര്യോധനൻ തിരിച്ചുവരുന്നു; കൗരവയോദ്ധാക്കളെല്ലാം വീണ്ടും അർജുനനെ വളയുന്നു. അർജുനൻ മരവിപ്പിക്കുന്ന അസ്ത്രം തൊടുക്കുന്നു; അവരെല്ലാം ബോധരഹിതരായി വീഴുന്നു. രാജകുമാരിയുടെ ആവശ്യം ഓർത്ത്, ദ്രോണർ, കൃപർ, കർണ്ണൻ, അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ്, ദുര്യോധനൻ എന്നിവരുടെ നല്ല മേൽവസ്ത്രങ്ങൾ എടുക്കാൻ ഉത്തരനെ അയയ്ക്കുന്നു. പ്രതിരോധമന്ത്രം അറിയുന്ന ഭീഷ്മരെ വെറുതെ വിട്ട്, അദ്ദേഹം വീട്ടിലേക്ക് തിരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आहूयमानस्तु स तेन संख्ये\nमहामना धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रः ।\nनिवर्तितस्तस्य गिराङ्कुशेन\nगजो यथा मत्त इवाङ्कुशेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Challenged thus in battle, the great-minded son of Dhritarashtra was turned back by those words, as a rutting elephant is turned by the goad."}},{"n":2,"text":"सोऽमृष्यमाणो वचसाभिमृष्टो\nमहारथेनातिरथस्तरस्वी ।\nपर्याववर्ताथ रथेन वीरो\nभोगी यथा पादतलाभिमृष्टः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unable to bear the speech, the great chariot-warrior, that mighty hero, wheeled his chariot around, like a snake trodden underfoot."}},{"n":3,"text":"तं प्रेक्ष्य कर्णः परिवर्तमानं\nनिवर्त्य संस्तभ्य च विद्धगात्रः ।\nदुर्योधनं दक्षिणतोऽभ्यगच्छ-\nत्पार्थं नृवीरो युधि हेममाली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him turn back, Karna, his body wounded, rallied and steadied himself, and that gold-garlanded hero went up to Partha on Duryodhana's right."}},{"n":4,"text":"भीष्मस्ततः शांतनवो निवृत्य\nहिरण्यकक्ष्यांस्त्वरयंस्तुरंगान् ।\nदुर्योधनं पश्चिमतोऽभ्यरक्ष-\nत्पार्थान्महाबाहुरधिज्यधन्वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, son of Shantanu, also turned back, urging on his gold-harnessed horses, and with bow strung guarded Duryodhana on the west against Partha."}},{"n":5,"text":"द्रोणः कृपश्चैव विविंशतिश्च\nदुःशासनश्चैव निवृत्य शीघ्रम् ।\nसर्वे पुरस्ताद्विततेषुचापा\nदुर्योधनार्थं त्वरिताभ्युपेयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, Kripa, Vivimshati and Duhshasana also turned back swiftly, and all came up in front with bows drawn to protect Duryodhana."}},{"n":6,"text":"स तान्यनीकानि निवर्तमाना-\nन्यालोक्य पूर्णौघनिभानि पार्थः ।\nहंसो यथा मेघमिवापतन्तं\nधनंजयः प्रत्यपतत्तरस्वी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those armies returning, like swollen floods, Dhananjaya the swift went against them, like a swan flying at an oncoming cloud."}},{"n":7,"text":"ते सर्वतः संपरिवार्य पार्थ-\nमस्त्राणि दिव्यानि समाददानाः ।\nववर्षुरभ्येत्य शरैः समन्ता-\nन्मेघा यथा भूधरमम्बुवेगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounding Partha on every side and taking up divine weapons, they rained arrows on him from all around, as clouds pour torrents on a mountain."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततोऽस्त्रमस्त्रेण निवार्य तेषां\nगाण्डीवधन्वा कुरुपुंगवानाम् ।\nसंमोहनं शत्रुसहोऽन्यदस्त्रं\nप्रादुश्चकारैन्द्रिरपारणीयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wielder of the Gandiva, Indra's son, checked their weapons with his weapon and brought forth another weapon, the bewildering one, which the foes could not withstand."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो दिशश्चानुदिशो विवृत्य\nशरैः सुधारैर्निशितैः सुपुङ्खैः ।\nगाण्डीवघोषेण मनांसि तेषां\nमहाबलः प्रव्यथयां चकार ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he opened up all the directions and intermediate directions with sharp, well-feathered arrows, and with the Gandiva's twang that mighty man shook their minds."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततः पुनर्भीमरवं प्रगृह्य\nदोर्भ्यां महाशङ्खमुदारघोषम् ।\nव्यनादयत्स प्रदिशो दिशः खं\nभुवं च पार्थो द्विषतां निहन्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, slayer of foes, Partha again took in both hands a great conch of dreadful sound and deep tone, and made it fill the quarters, the sky and the earth."}},{"n":11,"text":"ते शङ्खनादेन कुरुप्रवीराः\nसंमोहिताः पार्थसमीरितेन ।\nउत्सृज्य चापानि दुरासदानि\nसर्वे तदा शान्तिपरा बभूवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bewildered by that conch-blast sounded by Partha, all the Kuru heroes let go of their formidable bows and fell still."}},{"n":12,"text":"तथा विसंज्ञेषु परेषु पार्थः\nस्मृत्वा तु वाक्यानि तथोत्तरायाः ।\nनिर्याहि मध्यादिति मत्स्यपुत्र-\nमुवाच यावत्कुरवो विसंज्ञाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his foes unconscious, Partha remembered Uttara's words and said to the Matsya prince, \"Drive out from the middle, while the Kurus remain senseless.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"आचार्य शारद्वतयोः सुशुक्ले\nकर्णस्य पीतं रुचिरं च वस्त्रम् ।\nद्रौणेश्च राज्ञश्च तथैव नीले\nवस्त्रे समादत्स्व नरप्रवीर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Take the pure white clothes of the two teachers, Drona and Kripa, Karna's lovely yellow cloth, and the blue clothes of Drona's son and of the king, O hero among men.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"भीष्मस्य संज्ञां तु तथैव मन्ये\nजानाति मेऽस्त्रप्रतिघातमेषः ।\nएतस्य वाहान्कुरु सव्यतस्त्व-\nमेवं हि यातव्यममूढसंज्ञैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I think Bhishma is not bewildered, for he knows how to counter my weapon. Keep his horses on your left, and so pass by those whose senses are not clouded.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"रश्मीन्समुत्सृज्य ततो महात्मा\nरथादवप्लुत्य विराटपुत्रः ।\nवस्त्राण्युपादाय महारथानां\nतूर्णं पुनः स्वं रथमारुरोह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Letting go of the reins, the great-souled son of Virata leapt down from the chariot, quickly gathered the clothes of the great chariot-warriors, and climbed back into his own chariot."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततोऽन्वशासच्चतुरः सदश्वा-\nन्पुत्रो विराटस्य हिरण्यकक्ष्यान् ।\nते तद्व्यतीयुर्ध्वजिनामनीकं\nश्वेता वहन्तोऽर्जुनमाजिमध्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata's son directed the four fine horses with gold harness, and those white horses carried Arjuna through the banner-bearing host and out of the middle of the battle."}},{"n":17,"text":"तथा तु यान्तं पुरुषप्रवीरं\nभीष्मः शरैरभ्यहनत्तरस्वी ।\nस चापि भीष्मस्य हयान्निहत्य\nविव्याध पार्श्वे दशभिः पृषत्कैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that foremost hero went so, mighty Bhishma struck him with arrows, and Arjuna killed Bhishma's horses and pierced his side with ten shafts."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनो भीष्ममपास्य युद्धे\nविद्ध्वास्य यन्तारमरिष्टधन्वा ।\nतस्थौ विमुक्तो रथवृन्दमध्या-\nद्राहुं विदार्येव सहस्ररश्मिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, whose bow never failed, left Bhishma aside in battle after wounding his charioteer, and stood free from the mass of chariots, like the thousand-rayed sun that has burst out of Rahu."}},{"n":19,"text":"लब्ध्वा तु संज्ञां च कुरुप्रवीरः\nपार्थं समीक्ष्याथ महेन्द्रकल्पम् ।\nरणाद्विमुक्तं स्थितमेकमाजौ\nस धार्तराष्ट्रस्त्वरितो बभाषे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regaining his senses, the Kuru hero, seeing Partha like great Indra standing alone, free from the fight, Dhritarashtra's son quickly spoke."}},{"n":20,"text":"अयं कथं स्विद्भवतां विमुक्त-\nस्तं वै प्रबध्नीत यथा न मुच्येत् ।\nतमब्रवीच्छांतनवः प्रहस्य\nक्व ते गता बुद्धिरभूत्क्व वीर्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How has he escaped you? Bind him so that he cannot get away!\" Bhishma, son of Shantanu, laughed and said to him, \"Where were your wits and your strength?\""}},{"n":21,"text":"शान्तिं पराश्वस्य यथा स्थितोऽभू-\nरुत्सृज्य बाणांश्च धनुश्च चित्रम् ।\nन त्वेव बीभत्सुरलं नृशंसं\nकर्तुं न पापेऽस्य मनो निविष्टम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You stood still, calm, with your arrows and fine bow cast down. Bibhatsu would never do a cruel deed, and his mind is not set on wickedness.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"त्रैलोक्यहेतोर्न जहेत्स्वधर्मं\nतस्मान्न सर्वे निहता रणेऽस्मिन् ।\nक्षिप्रं कुरून्याहि कुरुप्रवीर\nविजित्य गाश्च प्रतियातु पार्थः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He would not give up his own duty even for the three worlds. That is why not all of us were killed in this battle. Quickly return, hero of the Kurus; let Partha go, having won the cattle.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तस्य तु तन्निशम्य\nपितामहस्यात्महितं वचोऽथ ।\nअतीतकामो युधि सोऽत्यमर्षी\nराजा विनिःश्वस्य बभूव तूष्णीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that grandfather's words, spoken for his own good, Duryodhana, his desire for battle gone, sighed in great anger and said nothing."}},{"n":24,"text":"तद्भीष्मवाक्यं हितमीक्ष्य सर्वे\nधनंजयाग्निं च विवर्धमानम् ।\nनिवर्तनायैव मनो निदध्यु-\nर्दुर्योधनं ते परिरक्षमाणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that Bhishma's counsel was wise, and Dhananjaya's fire growing, they all set their minds on turning back, guarding Duryodhana."}},{"n":25,"text":"तान्प्रस्थितान्प्रीतमनाः स पार्थो\nधनंजयः प्रेक्ष्य कुरुप्रवीरान् ।\nआभाषमाणोऽनुययौ मुहूर्तं\nसंपूजयंस्तत्र गुरून्महात्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them depart, the great-souled Dhananjaya, pleased, followed them a while, speaking to them and honoring his elders there."}},{"n":26,"text":"पितामहं शांतनवं स वृद्धं\nद्रोणं गुरुं च प्रतिपूज्य मूर्ध्ना ।\nद्रौणिं कृपं चैव गुरूंश्च सर्वा-\nञ्शरैर्विचित्रैरभिवाद्य चैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He honored the aged grandfather Bhishma and the teacher Drona with his head, and with varied arrows he saluted Drona's son, Kripa and all his elders."}},{"n":27,"text":"दुर्योधनस्योत्तमरत्नचित्रं\nचिच्छेद पार्थो मुकुटं शरेण ।\nआमन्त्र्य वीरांश्च तथैव मान्या-\nन्गाण्डीवघोषेण विनाद्य लोकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one arrow Partha cut Duryodhana's crown, bright with the finest jewels. Then taking leave of the heroes and honored ones, he made the worlds ring with the Gandiva's twang."}},{"n":28,"text":"स देवदत्तं सहसा विनाद्य\nविदार्य वीरो द्विषतां मनांसि ।\nध्वजेन सर्वानभिभूय शत्रू-\nन्स हेमजालेन विराजमानः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly sounding the Devadatta, that hero shattered the hearts of his foes, overwhelmed all enemies with his banner, and shone with its golden mesh."}},{"n":29,"text":"दृष्ट्वा प्रयातांस्तु कुरून्किरीटी\nहृष्टोऽब्रवीत्तत्र स मत्स्यपुत्रम् ।\nआवर्तयाश्वान्पशवो जितास्ते\nयाताः परे याहि पुरं प्रहृष्टः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Kurus depart, Kiritin joyfully said to the Matsya prince, \"Turn the horses. Your cattle are won, the enemies have gone; go to your city gladly.\""}}]}]}